module tokenizer

// keyword_hash.co -- sqlite3KeywordCode() as a hash table (perf2).
//
// SQLite's keywordCode() algorithm, literally: hash
//   ((charMap(first)*4) ^ (charMap(last)*3) ^ len) % 127,
// charMap(c) = c | 32, bucket chains, length check first,
// then a case-insensitive compare folding via (byte & 223)
// against uppercase text (SQLite's (c & ~0x20) with 223 = ~0x20
// masked to a byte). Pre-reject: len < 2 or len > 17.
//
// Tables generated from sqlite-ref gen/keywordhash.h (buckets,
// chains, lengths, offsets, packed text) + co_SQLite
// keywords.co (name -> TK_* code, matched by name). Chain
// order is SQLite's (converted 1-based -> 0-based, 0 -> -1).
// The substring packing of zKWText is kept (666 bytes); only
// the lookup is new. No map, no allocation, no ERR: a miss
// returns TK_ID without touching ERR (the old lookup_lower
// path set ERR(ENOENT) on every miss and cleared it).
//
// Packed int[] layout (715 ints): buckets [0..126],
// next [127..273], lens [274..420], offsets [421..567],
// codes [568..714].
